<title>JAPAN: Honma Golf jumps on earnings, share repurchase.</title>
<headline>Honma Golf jumps on earnings, share repurchase.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-05-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Honma Golf Co Ltd shares jumped on Thursday morning after the firm announced healthy earnings and also plans to repurchase some of its shares on Wednesday, brokers said.</p>
<p>As of 0048 GMT, shares in the golf club and golf wear maker stood at 2,000 in over-the-counter trade, after finishing at 1,850 on Wednesday.  </p>
<p>On Wednesday, Honma said its parent current profit in the year ending March 1997 was 7.65 billion yen, up from 6.07 billion in the previous year.</p>
<p>The firm also said it was planning to repurchase up to 3.10934 million of its shares.</p>
